Subject: [PATCH] render: keep reference frame buffers when rendering fails

decode_and_render_hf_groups() moves the buffers of a frame that is saved as a
reference (or as an LF frame) out of the frame while it renders into them, and
only moved them back at the end: any error returned in between dropped them.
Callers may ignore a failed flush_pixels() and keep decoding (the progressive
fuzzer does), and the next render then panicked looking up the missing buffers
(low_memory_pipeline: index out of bounds in check_buffer_sizes). Move the
buffers back on errors too. Test:
test_fuzzer_failed_flush_keeps_reference_frame_buffers.

diff --git a/jxl/src/frame/render.rs b/jxl/src/frame/render.rs
